IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc18-soira-offences.l4 -- the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, sections 490.03 to 490.032 (disclosure of the registered information, the offences of
-- not complying with an order or obligation, of giving false information and of not advising a police service, the warrant to arrest, and the regulations).
-- Part agent ccc18; layer 1. Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN (or MAYBE of a type): JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words), NOTHING (not covered); an offence
-- whose elements are not all met answers NOTHING ("without reasonable excuse" limits the prohibition in its own wording: the text does not say the person is innocent of
-- every other offence). The Sex Offender Information Registration Act is not among the sources: what it provides is taken as an input. See `ccc18-soira-notice` and NOTES.md.

§ `Sections 490.03 to 490.032 -- Disclosure, offences, warrant, regulations`

§ `490.03 Disclosure of information`

-- src:10585 | Disclosure of Information
-- src:10586 | Disclosure
-- src:10587 | 490.03 (1) The Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or a person authorized by the Commissioner shall, on request, disclose information that is registered in the database or the fact that such information is registered in the database
-- src:10588 | (a) to the prosecutor if the disclosure is necessary for the purpose of a proceeding under section 490.012; or
-- src:10589 | (b) to the Attorney General if the disclosure is necessary for the purpose of a proceeding under section 490.016, 490.023, 490.027, 490.02905, 490.029051, 490.02909, 490.029111, 490.029112, 490.02913, 490.04 or 490.05 or for the purpose of an appeal from a decision made in any of those proceedings or in a proceeding under section 490.012 or 490.013.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.03(1) (src:10585-10589)
DECLARE `s 490.03(1) recipient` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.03(1) the prosecutor`
    `s 490.03(1) the Attorney General`
    `s 490.03(1) another person`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.03(1) (src:10585-10589)
GIVEN recipient IS A `s 490.03(1) recipient`
      `a request is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is necessary for the purpose of the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is under the section` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the disclosure is for the purpose of an appeal from a decision made in the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.03(1) the Commissioner or a person authorized by the Commissioner shall, on request, disclose the registered information` MEANS
    CONSIDER recipient
    WHEN `s 490.03(1) the prosecutor` THEN
        IF `a request is made` AND `the disclosure is necessary for the purpose of the proceeding` AND `the proceeding is under the section`'s `section` EQUALS 490.012 AND (NOT `the disclosure is for the purpose of an appeal from a decision made in the proceeding`)
        THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a) a proceeding under section 490.012
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to the prosecutor if the disclosure is necessary for the purpose of a proceeding under section 490.012" [marginal (a)]
    WHEN `s 490.03(1) the Attorney General` THEN
        IF `a request is made` AND `the disclosure is necessary for the purpose of the proceeding`
           AND (  (   `the proceeding is under the section`'s `section` EQUALS 490.016 OR `the proceeding is under the section`'s `section` EQUALS 490.023 OR `the proceeding is under the section`'s `section` EQUALS 490.027
                   OR `the proceeding is under the section`'s `section` EQUALS 490.02905 OR `the proceeding is under the section`'s `section` EQUALS 490.029051 OR `the proceeding is under the section`'s `section` EQUALS 490.02909
                   OR `the proceeding is under the section`'s `section` EQUALS 490.029111 OR `the proceeding is under the section`'s `section` EQUALS 490.029112 OR `the proceeding is under the section`'s `section` EQUALS 490.02913
                   OR `the proceeding is under the section`'s `section` EQUALS 490.04 OR `the proceeding is under the section`'s `section` EQUALS 490.05)
               OR (`the disclosure is for the purpose of an appeal from a decision made in the proceeding` AND (`the proceeding is under the section`'s `section` EQUALS 490.012 OR `the proceeding is under the section`'s `section` EQUALS 490.013)))
        THEN JUST TRUE   -- (b) a proceeding under section 490.016, 490.023, 490.027, 490.02905, 490.029051, 490.02909, 490.029111, 490.029112, 490.02913, 490.04 or 490.05, or an appeal from a decision in any of those proceedings or in a proceeding under section 490.012 or 490.013
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to the Attorney General if the disclosure is necessary for the purpose of a proceeding under section 490.016" [marginal (a)]
    WHEN `s 490.03(1) another person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is to disclose "(a) to the prosecutor" and "(b) to the Attorney General"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.03(1) (src:10585-10589)
DECLARE `s 490.03(1) party` IS ONE OF `s 490.03(1) the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or a person authorized by the Commissioner`   -- not in the core's Party: NEEDS-CORE.md
DECLARE `s 490.03(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.03(1) disclose, on request, information that is registered in the database, or the fact that such information is registered, to the prosecutor`
    `s 490.03(1) disclose, on request, information that is registered in the database, or the fact that such information is registered, to the Attorney General`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.03(1) (src:10585-10589)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 490.03(1) party` `s 490.03(1) action`
`s 490.03(1)(a) the duty of the Commissioner to disclose to the prosecutor` MEANS
    PARTY `s 490.03(1) the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or a person authorized by the Commissioner`
    MUST `s 490.03(1) disclose, on request, information that is registered in the database, or the fact that such information is registered, to the prosecutor`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 490.03(1) the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or a person authorized by the Commissioner` BECAUSE "the information was not disclosed to the prosecutor on request"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.03(1) (src:10585-10589)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 490.03(1) party` `s 490.03(1) action`
`s 490.03(1)(b) the duty of the Commissioner to disclose to the Attorney General` MEANS
    PARTY `s 490.03(1) the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or a person authorized by the Commissioner`
    MUST `s 490.03(1) disclose, on request, information that is registered in the database, or the fact that such information is registered, to the Attorney General`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 490.03(1) the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or a person authorized by the Commissioner` BECAUSE "the information was not disclosed to the Attorney General on request"

-- src:10590 | Disclosure in connection with proceedings
-- src:10591 | (2) The Commissioner or that person shall, on request, disclose to the prosecutor or Attorney General the information that is registered in the database relating to a person if the person discloses, in connection with a proceeding or appeal other than one referred to in subsection (1), the fact that information relating to them is registered in the database.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.03(2) (src:10590-10591)
GIVEN `a request is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person discloses, in connection with a proceeding or appeal other than one referred to in subsection (1), the fact that information relating to them is registered in the database` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.03(2) the Commissioner or a person authorized by the Commissioner shall, on request, disclose the information to the prosecutor or Attorney General` MEANS
    IF `a request is made` AND `the person discloses, in connection with a proceeding or appeal other than one referred to in subsection (1), the fact that information relating to them is registered in the database`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall, on request, disclose to the prosecutor or Attorney General the information that is registered in the database relating to a person if the person discloses" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.03(2) (src:10590-10591)
DECLARE `s 490.03(2) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.03(2) disclose, on request, to the prosecutor or Attorney General the information that is registered in the database relating to the person`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.03(2) (src:10590-10591)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 490.03(1) party` `s 490.03(2) action`
`s 490.03(2) the duty of the Commissioner to disclose to the prosecutor or Attorney General` MEANS
    PARTY `s 490.03(1) the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or a person authorized by the Commissioner`
    MUST `s 490.03(2) disclose, on request, to the prosecutor or Attorney General the information that is registered in the database relating to the person`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 490.03(1) the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or a person authorized by the Commissioner` BECAUSE "the information was not disclosed on request"

-- src:10592 | Disclosure in proceedings
-- src:10593 | (3) The prosecutor or the Attorney General may, if the information is relevant to the proceeding, appeal or any subsequent appeal, disclose it to the presiding court.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.03(3) (src:10592-10593)
GIVEN `the information is relevant to the proceeding, appeal or any subsequent appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.03(3) the prosecutor or the Attorney General may disclose the information to the presiding court` MEANS
    IF `the information is relevant to the proceeding, appeal or any subsequent appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the permission is given "if the information is relevant to the proceeding, appeal or any subsequent appeal" (fork F5: the other reading is JUST FALSE)

§ `490.031 Offence; reasonable excuse; proof by certificate`

-- src:10596 | Offences
-- src:10597 | Offence
-- src:10598 | 490.031 (1) Every person who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with an order made under section 490.012 or under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act or with an obligation under section 490.019 or 490.02901, under section 227.06 of the National Defence Act or under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act is guilty of an offence and liable
-- src:10599 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine of not more than $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years, or to both; or
-- src:10600 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine of not more than $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day, or to both.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.031(1) (src:10596-10600)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with an order made under section 490.012 or under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act or with an obligation under section 490.019 or 490.02901, under section 227.06 of the National Defence Act or under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.031(1) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person fails to comply with an order made under section 490.012 or under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act or with an obligation under section 490.019 or 490.02901, under section 227.06 of the National Defence Act or under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act`
       AND (NOT `the person has a reasonable excuse`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is that of a person who, "without reasonable excuse, fails to comply"; outside it the subsection says nothing of liability

@ref Criminal Code s 490.031(1) (src:10596-10600)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 490.031(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`   -- "guilty of an offence and liable (a) on conviction on indictment ... or (b) on summary conviction"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.031(1) (src:10596-10600)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 490.031(1)(a) the punishment on conviction on indictment` MEANS Punishment WITH
    `mode` IS `by indictment`
    `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`
    `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
    `maximum fine` IS `a fine of` 10000
    `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`   -- "to a fine of not more than $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years, or to both": no minimum is stated

@ref Criminal Code s 490.031(1) (src:10596-10600)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 490.031(1)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS Punishment WITH
    `mode` IS `on summary conviction`
    `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`
    `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
    `maximum fine` IS `a fine of` 10000
    `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

-- src:10601 | Reasonable excuse
-- src:10602 | (2) For greater certainty, a lawful command that prevents a person from complying with an order or obligation is a reasonable excuse if, at the time, the person is subject to the Code of Service Discipline within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the National Defence Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.031(2) (src:10601-10602)
GIVEN `a lawful command prevents the person from complying with an order or obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time, the person is subject to the Code of Service Discipline within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the National Defence Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.031(2) a lawful command is a reasonable excuse` MEANS
    IF `a lawful command prevents the person from complying with an order or obligation` AND `at the time, the person is subject to the Code of Service Discipline within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the National Defence Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For greater certainty" a lawful command "is a reasonable excuse if, at the time, the person is subject to the Code of Service Discipline"; the text does not say that in no other case is it one (fork F9)

-- src:10603 | Proof of certain facts by certificate
-- src:10604 | (3) In proceedings under subsection (1), a certificate of a person referred to in paragraph 16(2)(b) of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act stating that the sex offender failed to report under section 4, 4.1, 4.2 or 4.3 — or provide information under section 5 or notify a person under subsection 6(1) or (1.01) — of that Act is evidence of the statements contained in it without proof of the signature or official character of the person appearing to have signed it.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.031(3) (src:10603-10604)
GIVEN `the proceedings are under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a certificate of a person referred to in paragraph 16(2)(b) of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that the sex offender failed to report under section 4, 4.1, 4.2 or 4.3, or to provide information under section 5, or to notify a person under subsection 6(1) or (1.01), of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.031(3) the certificate is evidence of the statements contained in it without proof of the signature or official character` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are under subsection (1)` AND `it is a certificate of a person referred to in paragraph 16(2)(b) of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` AND `it states that the sex offender failed to report under section 4, 4.1, 4.2 or 4.3, or to provide information under section 5, or to notify a person under subsection 6(1) or (1.01), of that Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In proceedings under subsection (1), a certificate of a person referred to in paragraph 16(2)(b) of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act stating that the sex offender failed to report under section 4"

-- src:10605 | Attendance and cross-examina­tion
-- src:10606 | (4) The sex offender named in the certificate may, with the leave of the court, require the attendance of the person who signed it for the purpose of cross-examination.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.031(4) (src:10605-10606)
GIVEN `the person is the sex offender named in the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court gives leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.031(4) the sex offender may require the attendance of the person who signed the certificate for cross-examination` MEANS
    IF `the person is the sex offender named in the certificate` AND `the court gives leave` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The sex offender named in the certificate may, with the leave of the court, require the attendance"

-- src:10607 | Notice of intention to produce
-- src:10608 | (5) A certificate is not to be received in evidence unless, before the commencement of the trial, the party who intends to produce it gives the sex offender a copy of it and reasonable notice of their intention to produce it.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.031(5) (src:10607-10608)
GIVEN `before the commencement of the trial, the party who intends to produce the certificate gives the sex offender a copy of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `before the commencement of the trial, the party who intends to produce the certificate gives the sex offender reasonable notice of their intention to produce it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.031(5) the certificate is not to be received in evidence` MEANS
    IF `before the commencement of the trial, the party who intends to produce the certificate gives the sex offender a copy of it` AND `before the commencement of the trial, the party who intends to produce the certificate gives the sex offender reasonable notice of their intention to produce it`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A certificate is not to be received in evidence unless, before the commencement of the trial, the party who intends to produce it gives the sex offender a copy of it and reasonable notice"
    ELSE JUST TRUE   -- the bar applies: "is not to be received in evidence unless"

§ `490.0311 Offence: false or misleading information`

-- src:10609 | Offence
-- src:10610 | 490.0311 Every person who knowingly provides false or misleading information under subsection 5(1) or 6(1) or (1.01) of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act is guilty of an offence and liable
-- src:10611 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine of not more than $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years, or to both; or
-- src:10612 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine of not more than $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day, or to both.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.0311 (src:10609-10612)
GIVEN `the person knowingly provides false or misleading information under subsection 5(1) or 6(1) or (1.01) of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.0311 the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person knowingly provides false or misleading information under subsection 5(1) or 6(1) or (1.01) of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is that of a person who "knowingly provides false or misleading information under subsection 5(1) or 6(1) or (1.01)"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.0311 (src:10609-10612)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 490.0311 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.0311 (src:10609-10612)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 490.0311(a) the punishment on conviction on indictment` MEANS Punishment WITH
    `mode` IS `by indictment`
    `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`
    `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
    `maximum fine` IS `a fine of` 10000
    `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.0311 (src:10609-10612)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 490.0311(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS Punishment WITH
    `mode` IS `on summary conviction`
    `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`
    `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
    `maximum fine` IS `a fine of` 10000
    `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

§ `490.0312 Offence: not advising a police service`

-- src:10613 | Offence
-- src:10614 | 490.0312 Every person who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with an obligation under subsection 490.02911(1) or (2) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.0312 (src:10613-10614)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with an obligation under subsection 490.02911(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.0312 the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person fails to comply with an obligation under subsection 490.02911(1) or (2)` AND (NOT `the person has a reasonable excuse`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is that of a person who, "without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with an obligation under subsection 490.02911(1) or (2)"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.0312 (src:10613-10614)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 490.0312 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.0312 (src:10613-10614)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 490.0312 the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS Punishment WITH
    `mode` IS `on summary conviction`
    `maximum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`   -- the section states no penalty: the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction is in another part (section 787), not among the sources
    `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
    `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
    `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

§ `490.03121 Warrant to arrest`

-- src:10616 | Warrant
-- src:10617 | Warrant to arrest
-- src:10618 | 490.03121 (1) If a justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that a person has contravened any of sections 4 to 5.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, the justice may issue a warrant in Form 6.4 authorizing a peace officer to arrest the person and, despite section 7.1 of that Act, bring them to any registration centre to remedy the contravention.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.03121(1) (src:10616-10618)
GIVEN `the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person has contravened any of sections 4 to 5.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.03121(1) the justice may issue a warrant in Form 6.4 to arrest the person` MEANS
    IF `the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person has contravened any of sections 4 to 5.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that a person has contravened any of sections 4 to 5.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, the justice may issue a warrant in Form 6.4" (fork F5: the other reading is JUST FALSE)

@ref Criminal Code s 490.03121(1) (src:10616-10618)
DECLARE `s 490.03121(1) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.03121(1) issue a warrant in Form 6.4 authorizing a peace officer to arrest the person and bring them to any registration centre to remedy the contravention`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.03121(1) (src:10616-10618)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.03121(1) action`
`s 490.03121(1) the power of the justice to issue the warrant` MEANS
    PARTY `a justice`
    MAY `s 490.03121(1) issue a warrant in Form 6.4 authorizing a peace officer to arrest the person and bring them to any registration centre to remedy the contravention`
    HENCE FULFILLED

